---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="The Bala Regatta has been held at the Township Dock in Bala, Muskoka for more than a century, presented by the Bala Aquatic Association."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>A Muskoka summer fixture</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Bala Regatta has been held at the Township Dock for more than a hundred years,
        presented by the Bala Aquatic Association.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens on the day</h2>
      <p>
        The morning belongs to the swimmers. Prizes are presented as soon as the swimming
        events finish, and the boating card follows straight on from there, opening with the
        punt races. A BBQ tent runs through the day.
      </p>
      <p>
        Entry is open to everyone. There are events for small children, events for
        sixteen-and-unders, events that put three generations of a family in the same canoe,
        and a few that exist mainly to be funny.
      </p>

      <h2>The association</h2>
      <p>
        The regatta is organised by volunteers of the Bala Aquatic Association, and paid for
        by <a href={href('/sponsors')}>local businesses</a> who sponsor the prizes and the day
        itself.
      </p>

      <h2>The archive</h2>
      <p>
        We are building a searchable record of past regattas — winners, organising committees,
        programmes, photographs and press coverage. Much of it is still to be transcribed from
        paper. <a href={href('/archives')}>Browse what is there so far</a>, and please
        <a href={href('/archives/corrections')}>tell us</a> about anything missing or wrong.
      </p>

      <aside class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>To write before launch.</strong> This page needs the association's own words
          on its history and founding — the year of the first regatta, how the Township Dock
          site came to be used, and anything the committee wants said about the event's place
          in the village. The copy above is a scaffold, deliberately kept to claims that can be
          supported.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
